    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n31347" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἰσέρπω</span></b> , aor.
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἰσείρπῠσα,</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>to go into,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐσέρπει ἐς ἄνθρωπον ψυχή</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hp.
					<u>Vict.</u>
					1.7
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Cleom.</u>
				8
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐς τὸ ἱερὸν μὴ
			ἐσέρπεν</span> (
				Dor.
			
			inf.) <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				12(3).183
			</span></i>(Astypalaea, <span class="entity">iv/iii B.C.</span>); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διὰ τοῦ στομίου</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Luc.
					<u>DMort.</u>
					3.2
				</span></i>
			: c. dat., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φθόνος βραχέσιν εἰσερπύσας χωρίοις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ph.
					2.553
				</span></i>
			.</div>
